        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Who may touch the user&amp;#39;s code, the import, the images and the registry once import ships? One row per identity, one column per resource.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everything here is planned (CNP-158: CNP-237 analyzer, CNP-238 build, CNP-239 chart, CNP-240 links, CNP-241 UI, CNP-242 topology, CNP-243 MCP); existing rows kept for contrast.&lt;br&gt;Read a column: who can read a user&amp;#39;s repo. Argo CD has no cell there on purpose: it reads cnp-projects and infra-templates only (GI4).&lt;br&gt;CNP-Portal holds its own permissions on the repos a user picks; the CMP only mints read tokens for one repo from it. Residual risk accepted on 2026-11-13 (GI1).&lt;br&gt;Guests get nothing new. The AI agent acts with its user&amp;#39;s rights; import and link need the user&amp;#39;s confirmation, Apply is never autonomous.&lt;br&gt;Source: import design spec v2 (2026-11-13) · CMP core/roles.py, services/authz.py · v0.1 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="74" width="1084" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
